plymouth (24.004.60+git20250831.4a3c171d-0ubuntu10oaxaca1) stonking; urgency=medium

  * Ubuntu's 24.004.60+git20250831.4a3c171d-0ubuntu10 rebuilt for Oaxaca
    with one upstream patch, script-check-console-viewer.patch (plymouth
    commit 88c8dd8d, 2026-08-06, "script: check if console_viewer is
    enabled"): the script plugin's sprite refresh showed or hid each
    display's console viewer without checking that one exists, and a view has
    none when text rendering is unavailable (no label plugin) or
    plymouth.prefer-fbcon is set. plymouthd then crashed in
    script_lib_sprite_refresh -> ply_console_viewer_hide booting the
    Oaxaca live ISO on the Legion laptop (2026-10-11), which also hid
    casper's "remove the installation medium" prompt at shutdown. Ubuntu's
    snapshot predates the fix. debian/ is otherwise Ubuntu's.

